<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Molyvos</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mithymna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Molyvos, officially Mithymna, is a small town on the northern coast of the Greek island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>, on the site of the ancient city of Methymna. Built on a hillside below a medieval castle that was held by the Genoese Gattilusi lords and then by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, it is known for its stone houses and harbour. It is now one of the main tourist centres of the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/molyvos.jpg" alt="Molyvos" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph by Mike Peel (www.mikepeel.net). · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Molyvos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
